{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"7d2888eb5ed3dce9455e1a5c5de750e08ee013018d281166d10d57e34ecdfa1c","digest":{"component_or_area":"fetcher pagination (core inbound path)","key_entities":["src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetcher.py","fetcher._iter_pages","fetcher.collect","_build_snapshot","jira.search.views.default.max","SilentTruncationError","start_at","page_size","maxResults"],"problem_keywords":["pagination","truncation","silent data loss","page size mismatch","inbound snapshot"],"propositions":["fetcher._iter_pages terminates on a short page (len(page) < page_size) instead of an empty page, advancing by page_size rather than len(page), causing silent truncation of the inbound snapshot when Jira Data Center caps maxResults below the requested page size","measured against a client serving 250 issues with a 20-issue page cap, only 20 issues are recovered (92% silently lost) because the first truncated page is misinterpreted as the final page","the pager lacks an offset-stall guard and will loop indefinitely if a server ignores startAt and returns the same non-empty page repeatedly","the defect affects the shared core inbound path (not isolated to the DC adapter), so it impacts both the Cloud bridge and DC implementations"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787322173949939001,"uuid":"dbcd3ef2-a68c-4306-bfee-631e43e6fa54"}